// Layer contract for the expression pipeline, read top to bottom: the
// evaluator reduces a tree to a value, the parser runs the conversion
// that produces one, the syntax tree is what it hands back, the lexer
// feeds it, tokens are what the lexer emits, and errors sit beneath all
// of them because any stage may fail. A module may reach downward and
// nowhere else, so each entry lists the layers open to it and every
// other crate path is refused.
//
// Naming what is open rather than what is shut is what makes this file
// carry cycle-freedom between the layers: every crate-internal import
// points down the order, and a set of modules whose edges all point one
// way cannot close a loop. cargo-modules offers a cycle check that
// would say the same from the other side, and 0.26.0 cannot say it: the
// search runs across the item graph before any filter narrows it, and a
// type owning a method that names the type back is a loop at that
// width. Every crate with an impl block fails it, so the reading lives
// here until the tool narrows first.
//
// Import paths are matched as they are written, so each pattern accepts
// both the `crate::` prefix the sources use and the crate's own name.
// A list of what is open has to name the standard library too, which
// the deeper layers reach for as freely as the rest, and has to leave
// room for the empty path an import reports for its own braces. Every
// name inside those braces arrives on its own and spelled out in full,
// which is where the reading happens. Each entry covers the module's
// submodules along with the file itself, a reach being a reach whatever
// depth it is written at.
//
// A module with no entry here is not under the promise above, but
// nothing that is may import it, so it stays a leaf until someone
// writes its layer down. The evaluator is the first arrival over the
// parser and the top of the order for now. A formatter joins it there
// as a second consumer neither of them may see the other from, and the
// test helper module lands with a rule keeping every stage out of it.
(
    lints: [
        Module((
            name: "evaluator_over_the_parser",
            matches: Module("^proofhouse_rust_lib::evaluator(::|$)"),
            rules: [
                // Reducing a tree to a number takes the node types, a
                // way to get a tree out of text, and the failures
                // either step reports. Nothing above the parser is in
                // reach, which is what will keep this module and the
                // formatter apart once the second one is written.
                RestrictImports(
                    allowed_only: Some([
                        "^(crate|proofhouse_rust_lib)::(ast|parser|errors)(::|$)",
                        "^std(::|$)",
                        "^$",
                    ]),
                    denied: None,
                    severity: Error,
                ),
            ],
        )),
        Module((
            name: "parser_above_everything",
            matches: Module("^proofhouse_rust_lib::parser(::|$)"),
            rules: [
                // The whole conversion runs from here, so every stage
                // beneath is in reach and the list is all of them.
                // What it turns away is a module nobody has placed
                // yet, which would leave the top of the pipeline
                // resting on something with no layer of its own.
                RestrictImports(
                    allowed_only: Some([
                        "^(crate|proofhouse_rust_lib)::(ast|lexer|tokens|errors)(::|$)",
                        "^std(::|$)",
                        "^$",
                    ]),
                    denied: None,
                    severity: Error,
                ),
            ],
        )),
        Module((
            name: "syntax_tree_below_the_parser",
            matches: Module("^proofhouse_rust_lib::ast(::|$)"),
            rules: [
                // A tree of nodes is a value like any other. Producing
                // one takes a lexer and a parser; being one takes
                // neither, and the reach that would make it otherwise
                // is what closes the pipeline into a loop. Errors stay
                // open because a node may carry the position a failure
                // points at.
                RestrictImports(
                    allowed_only: Some([
                        "^(crate|proofhouse_rust_lib)::errors(::|$)",
                        "^std(::|$)",
                        "^$",
                    ]),
                    denied: None,
                    severity: Error,
                ),
            ],
        )),
        Module((
            name: "lexer_below_the_syntax_tree",
            matches: Module("^proofhouse_rust_lib::lexer(::|$)"),
            rules: [
                // Scanning text into tokens is settled before a tree
                // exists, so the tokens it emits and the failures it
                // raises are the whole of what it needs. Reading the
                // tree or the parser from here would make the first
                // half of the pipeline depend on the second.
                RestrictImports(
                    allowed_only: Some([
                        "^(crate|proofhouse_rust_lib)::(tokens|errors)(::|$)",
                        "^std(::|$)",
                        "^$",
                    ]),
                    denied: None,
                    severity: Error,
                ),
            ],
        )),
        Module((
            name: "tokens_below_the_lexer",
            matches: Module("^proofhouse_rust_lib::tokens(::|$)"),
            rules: [
                // The token types describe what a lexer produces
                // without knowing that a lexer is what produces them,
                // which leaves errors the one layer beneath them.
                // Whoever writes the next producer inherits the same
                // freedom.
                RestrictImports(
                    allowed_only: Some([
                        "^(crate|proofhouse_rust_lib)::errors(::|$)",
                        "^std(::|$)",
                        "^$",
                    ]),
                    denied: None,
                    severity: Error,
                ),
            ],
        )),
        Module((
            name: "errors_below_everything",
            matches: Module("^proofhouse_rust_lib::errors(::|$)"),
            rules: [
                // Every stage above reports failures through these
                // types, which leaves this module the one place with
                // no crate path open to it at all. An error type that
                // reached back for a token or a node would drag the
                // whole pipeline into whatever imports it.
                RestrictImports(
                    allowed_only: Some([
                        "^std(::|$)",
                        "^$",
                    ]),
                    denied: None,
                    severity: Error,
                ),
            ],
        )),
    ],
)
